PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation remains divided between 750 (the majority view) and 700. Both camps agree on a net wager difference of 600 points (+200 for one successful Grand Tichu versus -400 for two failed Grand Tichus). The sole point of contention is whether trick points are bounded within [0, 100], or if capturing only the Phoenix results in -25 points for the losing team and +125 points for the winning team. Because the written rules dictate summing the face values of captured cards without any explicit flooring mechanic, the exact algebraic summation of +125 and -25 strictly conserves the 100-point deck total. Consequently, the maximal possible value of X - Y is maintained at 750.
}

